ui-sliders-select-a-value-or-range-along-a-track-use-standard-centered-or-range-variants-show = Sliders select a value or range along a track. Use standard, centered, or range variants, show the full available range, and apply changes immediately.

ui-use-sliders-to-adjust-continuous-settings-such-as-volume-brightness-or-filter-intensity-ap = Use sliders to adjust continuous settings such as volume, brightness, or filter intensity. Apply every value change immediately so the result stays connected to the handle movement.

ui-standard-sliders-start-at-a-minimum-centered-sliders-place-zero-in-the-middle-range-slider = Standard sliders start at a minimum; centered sliders place zero in the middle; range sliders choose a minimum and maximum. Prefer horizontal range sliders to reduce cognitive effort.

ui-the-track-represents-the-full-available-range-the-active-section-runs-from-the-minimum-to = The track represents the full available range. The active section runs from the minimum to the handle, or between the two handles of a range slider. Values increase toward the trailing edge in the reading direction.

ui-move-the-handle-to-select-a-value-a-range-slider-has-separate-minimum-and-maximum-handles = Move the handle to select a value. A range slider has separate minimum and maximum handles. Each handle narrows during interaction.

ui-show-a-value-label-for-the-handle-being-adjusted-if-a-separate-field-shows-the-value-the-b = Show a value label for the handle being adjusted. If a separate field shows the value, the built-in label is optional. Keep an editable field synchronized with the slider and next in the tab order.

ui-stop-indicators = Stop indicators

ui-stops-represent-equally-spaced-available-values-and-the-handle-snaps-to-the-closest-stop-k = Stops represent equally spaced available values, and the handle snaps to the closest stop. Keep the track readable by avoiding excessive stops. End stops may be omitted only when another visual anchor gives at least 3:1 contrast.

ui-stops = Stops

ui-orientation = Orientation

ui-use-horizontal-or-vertical-standard-and-centered-sliders-to-fit-the-task-vertical-values-i = Use horizontal or vertical standard and centered sliders to fit the task. Vertical values increase from the bottom.

ui-inset-icon = Inset icon

ui-only-standard-sliders-in-m-l-or-xl-sizes-support-an-inset-icon-at-low-values-it-moves-to-t = Only standard sliders in M, L, or XL sizes support an inset icon. At low values it moves to the inactive track. Do not add inset icons to centered or range sliders.

ui-track-heights-are-xs-16dp-s-24dp-m-40dp-l-56dp-and-xl-96dp-active-and-inactive-tracks-use = Track heights are XS 16dp, S 24dp, M 40dp, L 56dp, and XL 96dp. Active and inactive tracks use the same size. Reserve XL for a page where the slider is the primary task.

ui-select-drag = Select & drag

ui-drag-the-handle-to-update-a-continuous-value-or-snap-between-stops = Drag the handle to update a continuous value or snap between stops.

ui-drag-a-continuous-value = Drag a continuous value

ui-select-jump = Select jump

ui-select-the-track-to-move-the-handle-to-that-position-or-the-nearest-stop = Select the track to move the handle to that position, or the nearest stop.

ui-jump-between-stops = Jump between stops

ui-select-arrow = Select & arrow

ui-tab-moves-focus-to-the-handle-arrow-keys-change-the-value-by-one-value-or-stop-indicator-h = Tab moves focus to the handle. Arrow keys change the value by one value or stop indicator. Hold Space while pressing an arrow key to change it by a larger interval. Home and End select the first and last values.

ui-assistive-technology-must-identify-each-slider-adjust-its-handle-along-the-range-and-repor = Assistive technology must identify each slider, adjust its handle along the range, and report the selected value. Range sliders expose both handles separately.

ui-price-range = Price range

ui-the-handle-narrows-and-the-value-appears-during-touch-pointer-or-keyboard-interaction = The handle narrows and the value appears during touch, pointer, or keyboard interaction.

ui-focus-and-navigation = Focus and navigation

ui-initial-focus-lands-on-the-handle-arrow-keys-adjust-its-value-without-requiring-pointer-pr = Initial focus lands on the handle. Arrow keys adjust its value without requiring pointer precision.

ui-the-end-of-the-inactive-track-needs-a-visual-anchor-with-at-least-3-1-contrast-against-the = The end of the inactive track needs a visual anchor with at least 3:1 contrast against the background. Use an end stop or a contrasting icon or label at the endpoint.

ui-moves-focus-to-the-slider-handle = Moves focus to the slider handle

ui-increase-and-decrease-the-value-by-one-value-or-one-stop-indicator = Increase and decrease the value by one value or one stop indicator

